// Synthetic PAN-OS records for layout variants; every value is invented. The
// column order follows the PAN-OS 11.1 syslog field descriptions:
// - AUTH: Authentication log fields; the Strata Logging Service Authentication
//   syslog example writes the type as `AUTH`.
//   https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/authentication-log-fields
// - START: Tunnel Inspection log fields, whose type column holds `START` or
//   `END`.
//   https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/tunnel-inspection-log-fields
// - CORRELATION: Correlated Events log fields, with separate source address
//   and source user columns.
//   https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/correlated-events-log-fields
// - CONFIG: Config log fields, once with the before and after change details
//   and once without them, as in the Strata Logging Service Config syslog
//   example.
//   https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/config-log-fields
//   https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/strata-logging-service/log-reference/common-logs/common-config-log/common-config-syslog-fields
// - TRAFFIC: Traffic log fields, once with SD-WAN link switches that PAN-OS
//   writes as an unquoted brace list with commas (Palo Alto knowledge base
//   article kA14u0000004LaOCAU), and once with two values beyond the
//   documented columns.
//   https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/traffic-log-fields
// - URL Filtering: the 125 columns of PAN-OS 10.1 and later, with response
//   headers and HTTP status code after the request headers.
//   https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/url-filtering-log-fields
